  "an2.21:2.1": "_Paṇḍita_ is normally used for a learned scholar, rather than a contemplative “sage”. Pali has many more terms for “a wise person” than does English, and it is not easy to distinguish the senses. “Astute” is meant to convey the sense of one who is observant and of sound judgment. In early Sanskrit it is a desirable quality of a daughter or son (Bṛhadāraṇyaka Upaniṣad 6.4.17–18), and is a synonym of _medhāvī_ (Chāndogya Upaniṣad 6.14.2) and _dhīra_ (Kaṭha Upaniṣad 2.5). ",
